<title>NORWAY: POLL-Christiania H1 profits seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-Christiania H1 profits seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse, Norway's second largest bank, is expected to post a first-half 1997 pre-tax operating profit of about 1.25 billion crowns, according to six analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>The corresponding figure for the first half of 1996 was 1.11 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Five analysts had a buy recommendation on the share and one said hold.</p>
<p>Christiania will present the figures on August 6.</p>
<p>				   (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>				   Expectations H1 1997</p>
<p>				 Average    Low     High     H1 1996</p>
<p> Net interest income	1,759     1,729  1,789     1,704</p>
<p> Non-interest income	  979	 925  1,046	 768</p>
<p> Non-interest expenses    1,598     1,569  1,615     1,494</p>
<p> Operating profit before</p>
<p> loan losses and profit</p>
<p> on long-term securities  1,139     1,071  1,195	 978</p>
<p> Operating profit	   1,245     1,171  1,302     1,111</p>
<p> Net profit		   1,182	 936  1,290     1,099</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)		  2.15	1.70   2.34     2.00</p>
<p> EPS 1997			3.66	2.70   4.00</p>
<p> EPS 1998			3.19	2.70   3.60</p>
<p> Dividend 1997		 1.39	1.20   1.60</p>
<p>NOTE - One brokerage used a different method for estimating the tax and put it higher than the others. Excluding the estimate of that brokerage, the projected net profit based on the other five estimates is 1.23 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, Alf Asklund +47 22 93 69 71</p>
